course: dictionary
lesson: 14823
title: Quickness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quickness is a noun, a thing you can have. It means being fast. It can mean speed in your body, speed in your thinking, or how fast you get cross. The context tells you which one. «The cat caught the mouse with great quickness.» The word cat and the act of catching show that quickness here means speed of movement.
explain: «Her quickness of mind helped her solve the puzzle.» The word mind is the clue: this quickness is about thinking fast and clearly, not running. «His quickness of temper meant he shouted at the smallest thing.» The words temper and shouted show that quickness here means getting angry fast.
explain: Quickness is an uncountable noun, so it has no plural. You say quickness, not quicknesses. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "With great speed" fits the cat sentence, so that meaning works.
fact: Quickness means being fast, or being fast to think or react.
fact: «Quickness» can mean speed in movement, like «the quickness of a cat».
fact: «Quickness of mind» means thinking and understanding fast.
fact: «Quickness of temper» means being easily stirred to anger.
fact: Quickness is uncountable: it does not have a plural form.
exercise: «The goalkeeper saved the penalty with great quickness.» What does quickness mean here? | A loud shout from the crowd | Being cold and wet | Slow, careful steps | *Speed of movement
exercise: «Her quickness of mind helped her solve the maths puzzle.» What does quickness of mind mean? | Running around the track | Being easily angry | *Thinking and understanding fast | Feeling sad for a long time
exercise: «Grandma said Tom's quickness of temper got him into trouble.» What does quickness of temper suggest? | Walking slowly | Being very patient | Sleeping late | *Getting angry fast
test: Find and copy the word from this sentence that names being fast: «The fox showed great quickness when it leapt the fence.» | fence | leapt | fox | *quickness
test: «She answered every question with quickness and was right each time.» What is quickness here? | Being tired | Being loud | Being slow and careful | *Being fast in thinking
exam: Which sentence uses quickness correctly? | The quicknesses of the lizard saved it from the cat. | Quick the lizard saved from the cat. | *The quickness of the lizard saved it from the cat. | The lizard quickness away from the cat.
